  "description": "Sukra Dhangdamajhi, a disari (Bonda shaman) from Malkangiri district, Odisha, India, talks about his practice. Gobardhan Panda, a researcher of the Bonda language, interviews him in Bonda with some Desia, the common language of the Bonda, Gutob, Odia and other local communities. Desia words are marked in quotes in the Odia subtitles, such as 'ନି-ନା, ସେରମୂଲ୍'. Prateek Pattanaik recorded it in 2018 for Remosam, a 2019 documentary by Subhashish Panigrahi. Part of the footage was used in the film, and Panigrahi edited and published it under the Munaremo project in 2024. Gobardhan Panda subtitled the Bonda in Odia, and Panigrahi translated the subtitles into English and edited the Odia.",
